      "content": "No, you should not give an antihistamine or wait overnight with non-blanching rashes and fever, as these actions do not address the potential underlying cause and could allow a serious infection to progress. A low fever and active play do not rule out severe illnesses like sepsis or meningitis, which can sometimes present with limited symptoms initially in young children. The \"all or nothing\" choice here is between seeking immediate professional care and risking a life-threatening delay; waiting for the spots to disappear or the fever to resolve on its own is unsafe advice in this scenario. Please contact your pediatrician, an urgent care doctor, or the ER immediately to get a proper examination and diagnosis.",
